LLVM masked.scatter with overlapping addresses is guaranteed to execute in order from the least-significant vector element to the most-significant vector element. Equivalently, it behaves like serial scalar stores:

```c
for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)
  if (mask[i])
    pointers[i] = values[i];
```

Therefore, if multiple active lanes target the same address, the highest-numbered active lane’s value is stored last and remains in memory.
